---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Testimonials preview | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Three ways to introduce testimonials on the contact page."
>
  <style>
    .preview-head {
      padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-5);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-head h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    }
    .preview-panel {
      padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-panel .panel-label {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }
    .preview-panel h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }

    /* ---- Option 1: stacked, red left-rule ---- */
    .testi-rule {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
    }
    .testi-rule .quote {
      display: block;
      padding: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-6);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .testi-rule .quote .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    }
    .testi-rule .quote .a {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ---- Option 2: grid of bordered cards ---- */
    .testi-cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .testi-cards .quote {
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
      position: relative;
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--paper);
    }
    .testi-cards .quote::before {
      content: '“';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: var(--space-5);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 3rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--accent);
      transform: translateY(-0.3rem);
    }
    .testi-cards .quote .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    }
    .testi-cards .quote .a {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ---- Option 3: single pull-quote, editorial ---- */
    .testi-editorial {
      max-width: 46ch;
    }
    .testi-editorial .quote {
      margin: 0;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .testi-editorial .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      line-height: 1.4;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
      position: relative;
    }
    .testi-editorial .q::before {
      content: '“';
      display: block;
      font-size: 3rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .testi-editorial .a {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }
  </style>

  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head preview-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Design preview</p>
      <h1>Three ways to show testimonials.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Same three quotes, three visual treatments. Placement: contact page,
        after the rates, before the form.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>

  <!-- Option 1 -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option one, stacked list">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">Option 1 · Stacked, red left-rule</p>
      <h2>Why people keep working with me</h2>
      <div class="testi-rule">
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Option 2 -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option two, cards grid">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">Option 2 · Bordered card grid</p>
      <h2>Why people keep working with me</h2>
      <div class="testi-cards">
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Option 3 -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option three, editorial pull quote">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">Option 3 · Editorial pull-quote</p>
      <div class="testi-editorial">
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p class="q">
            She names the decision you've been avoiding and gives you the
            frame to make it, then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
